WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.047
Mary did not miss her mother at all.

2
00:00:17.048 --> 00:00:20.284
After all she had not really known her mother.

3
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:25.217
So now, after the death of her parents, she thought only of herself.

4
00:00:25.218 --> 00:00:33.338
She hoped she was going to live with nice people who would let her do whatever she wanted.

5
00:00:33.339 --> 00:00:37.935
At first she was taken to the home of the local English minister.

6
00:00:37.936 --> 00:00:43.216
He had five children who were always quarreling and snatching toys from each other.

7
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:46.986
Mary hated staying at their crowded, messy house.

8
00:00:46.987 --> 00:00:54.131
She was so disagreeable to the children that, after the first day or two, nobody would play with her.

9
00:00:54.132 --> 00:00:57.967
One day Mary was playing by herself under a tree.

10
00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:03.395
She was pretending to make a garden, just as she had been doing the day cholera broke out.

11
00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:07.979
One of the little boys, Basil, stood nearby watching her.

12
00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:13.438
"You are going to be sent home at the end of the week," Basil said to her.

13
00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:16.874
"And we're all glad about it."

14
00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:21.825
"I'm glad too," answered Mary. "Where is home?"

15
00:01:21.826 --> 00:01:26.684
"You don't know where home is?" Basil said scornfully.

16
00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:28.744
"It's England of course.

17
00:01:28.745 --> 00:01:34.155
You are going to live with your uncle, Mr. Archibald Craven."

18
00:01:34.156 --> 00:01:38.542
Mary frowned. "I don't know anything about him."

19
00:01:38.543 --> 00:01:43.979
"Of course you don't. You don't know anything," said Basil.

20
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.978
"But I heard Father and Mother talking about him.

21
00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:53.544
He lives in a big, old house called Misselthwaite Manor.

22
00:01:53.545 --> 00:02:00.203
No one goes near him. He's a hunchback and he's horrid."

23
00:02:00.204 --> 00:02:02.527
"I don't believe you."

24
00:02:02.528 --> 00:02:08.681
Mary turned her back and stuck her fingers in her ears because she didn't want to hear any more.

25
00:02:08.682 --> 00:02:11.947
But she thought it over a great deal afterward.

26
00:02:11.948 --> 00:02:16.860
What sort of place was she going to? What would her uncle be like?

27
00:02:16.861 --> 00:02:21.814
What was a hunchback anyway? What did one look like?

28
00:02:21.815 --> 00:02:29.532
Mary made the long voyage to England under the care of an officer's wife who was taking her children to boarding school.

29
00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:35.279
The officer's wife was too busy with her own little boy and girl to pay much attention to Mary.

30
00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:43.105
In London the officer's wife handed Mary over to Mrs. Medlock, the woman who was the housekeeper at Misselthwaite Manor.

31
00:02:43.106 --> 00:02:48.780
"My word! She's a plain little thing!" exclaimed Mrs. Medlock.

32
00:02:48.781 --> 00:02:51.901
"And we'd heard her mother was a beauty."

33
00:02:51.902 --> 00:02:56.708
"Perhaps she will improve as she grows older," said the officer's wife.

34
00:02:56.709 --> 00:03:04.932
The two women thought that Mary could not hear them because she was standing a little apart from them, but she heard every word.

35
00:03:04.933 --> 00:03:10.365
She thought Mrs. Medlock was the most disagreeable-looking woman she had ever seen.

36
00:03:10.366 --> 00:03:14.059
The next day they had to catch the train to Yorkshire.

37
00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.722
When they walked through the station, Mary tried to keep as far away from her as possible.

38
00:03:19.723 --> 00:03:24.571
She did not want anyone to think that she was Mrs. Medlock's daughter.

39
00:03:24.572 --> 00:03:31.328
Once they were settled on the train, Mrs. Medlock said, "Do you know anything about your uncle?"

40
00:03:31.329 --> 00:03:34.154
"No," Mary replied.

41
00:03:34.155 --> 00:03:37.255
"Well," said Mrs. Medlock.

42
00:03:37.256 --> 00:03:41.633
"I suppose you should be told something to prepare yourself.

43
00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:45.341
You are going to a strange place."

44
00:03:45.342 --> 00:03:46.992
Mary said nothing.

45
00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:51.662
She didn't care what this awful woman had to say about her uncle's house.

46
00:03:51.663 --> 00:03:56.918
"The house is six hundred years old," said Mrs. Medlock.

47
00:03:56.919 --> 00:04:05.329
"It's on the edge of the moor, and there are nearly a hundred rooms, though most of them are closed up and locked."

48
00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.180
Mary began to listen.

49
00:04:07.181 --> 00:04:11.854
It sounded so different from India, and anything new interested her.

50
00:04:11.855 --> 00:04:14.682
But she did not want to look interested.

51
00:04:14.683 --> 00:04:19.884
"Mr. Craven has a crooked back," Mrs. Medlock went on.

52
00:04:19.885 --> 00:04:28.095
"He was a sour young man, and did nothing good with his money and his big house until he married."

53
00:04:28.096 --> 00:04:30.909
Now Mary was really interested.

54
00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.321
She'd never thought of a hunchback as married.

55
00:04:34.322 --> 00:04:40.404
"His wife was a sweet, pretty thing, and he would have done anything for her.

56
00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:43.950
People said she married him for his money, but she didn't.

57
00:04:43.951 --> 00:04:46.636
And when she died . . ."

58
00:04:46.637 --> 00:04:50.031
"She died?" Mary exclaimed.

59
00:04:50.032 --> 00:04:55.421
She remembered a fairy tale about a poor hunchback and a beautiful princess.

60
00:04:55.422 --> 00:04:58.668
Suddenly she felt sorry for Mr. Craven.

61
00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:05.182
"Yes, she died," said Mrs. Medlock. "And that made him even stranger.

62
00:05:05.183 --> 00:05:10.516
He cares about nobody. He won't see people.

63
00:05:10.517 --> 00:05:18.179
Most of the time he travels, but when he's at Misselthwaite Manor, he shuts himself up in the west wing.

64
00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.991
He won't let anybody near him but his old servant, Pitcher."

65
00:05:22.992 --> 00:05:32.946
Mrs. Medlock was right. Mary was going to a strange place indeed.
